# Milestone: v0.10.15-vm-decomp-2
# Covers: v0.10.9-B — OP_PUSH_TAG binds the `t:` scope to the user tag t, so the
#         strand running inside `t: { ... }` is a member of t.  t.stop() from
#         inside is then a clean in-scope tag-stop on t's OWN active scope (NOT
#         the D3 "no active scope" fatal that an anonymous, unbound scope forced
#         pre-v0.10.15): the scope block evaluates to nil and the post-stop
#         write is skipped, so Realm.hit stays 0.
# matrix-row: tag-scope-binding
#
# Minimal pin (no try/catch/finally) — depends only on user-tag→scope-tag
# binding.  tag-stop "absorption" (resume AFTER the scope) is the separate,
# deferred T29 concern and is not exercised here.
var t = Tag.new()
Realm.hit = 0
t: { t.stop(); Realm.hit = 1 }
Realm.hit
[00000000] <Tag>
[00000000] 0
[00000000] nil
[00000001] 0
